WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:10.642
Rachel Okafor: Hi Luis, thanks for grabbing the time. How's your week going over there?

2
00:00:11.196 --> 00:00:17.924
Luis Ortega: Hey Rachel. Busy, but that's normal for September. We're heading into storm season, so claims volume is starting to climb.

3
00:00:18.893 --> 00:00:30.227
Rachel Okafor: Makes sense. I saw the call volume ticked up about twelve percent month over month across your tracking numbers. Is that the storm activity or just seasonal?

4
00:00:30.809 --> 00:00:40.518
Luis Ortega: Mostly seasonal, plus the new home bundle campaign that marketing launched on the fifteenth. That one's been driving a lot of after-hours calls.

5
00:00:41.572 --> 00:00:50.978
Rachel Okafor: Okay so that brings me to something I wanted to check in on. How's the AI Voice Agent pilot going on the after-hours claims intake?

6
00:00:51.467 --> 00:01:02.661
Luis Ortega: Mostly good. It's catching calls that would have gone to voicemail, and the transcripts are way better than I expected. But there's one thing that's been bugging my team.

7
00:01:03.697 --> 00:01:04.959
Rachel Okafor: Tell me more.

8
00:01:06.247 --> 00:01:15.924
Luis Ortega: When the AI agent transfers over to one of our live reps, the information it gathered doesn't show up on the Genesys screen.

9
00:01:15.924 --> 00:01:25.180
Luis Ortega: So the rep is starting from scratch, and the caller has to repeat their account number or policy number all over again.

10
00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.284
Luis Ortega: It makes us look disorganized.

11
00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:32.214
Rachel Okafor: Got it. Does that happen on every transfer, or only some of them?

12
00:01:32.546 --> 00:01:43.633
Luis Ortega: Every transfer I've listened to so far, which is maybe a dozen calls. My supervisor pulled a few recordings this week and saw the same thing.

13
00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:53.303
Rachel Okafor: And when you say the information doesn't show up, is that the AI's summary, or the raw details like name and claim number?

14
00:01:53.892 --> 00:02:03.253
Luis Ortega: Both, really. The rep sees the incoming call but nothing the agent collected. No name, no policy, no reason for the call.

15
00:02:03.484 --> 00:02:14.126
Rachel Okafor: Okay, let me take that back to the team and see what we're working with. Can you send me two or three call IDs from this week?

16
00:02:14.126 --> 00:02:14.914
Rachel Okafor: That'll help.

17
00:02:15.898 --> 00:02:21.147
Luis Ortega: Sure, I'll pull them this afternoon. I've got a list in the pilot tracker.

18
00:02:22.404 --> 00:02:26.759
Rachel Okafor: Perfect. Anything else on the pilot side? How's the after-hours coverage looking?

19
00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:34.545
Luis Ortega: Coverage is fine. We've got two new hires starting on the twenty-eighth, so that'll help with the queue once they're trained.

20
00:02:35.129 --> 00:02:41.228
Rachel Okafor: Nice. Are they going through the standard onboarding, or something different for the after-hours team?

21
00:02:42.222 --> 00:02:48.604
Luis Ortega: Standard. My team lead is handling it. They'll shadow for a week and then take live calls.

22
00:02:49.951 --> 00:02:59.636
Rachel Okafor: Good. Let me know if you want a refresher on the QM scorecards for that group. I know the new hires will be scored on the claims intake card.

23
00:03:00.007 --> 00:03:04.253
Luis Ortega: That's probably fine. The scorecards have been working well. No complaints there.

24
00:03:04.714 --> 00:03:12.546
Rachel Okafor: Good to hear. And what about the Google Ads side? Any shifts in spend you want me to know about?

25
00:03:13.689 --> 00:03:18.767
Luis Ortega: Not really. Marketing handles that. They mentioned they're happy with the offline conversion match rates.

26
00:03:19.544 --> 00:03:31.625
Rachel Okafor: Okay. I'll leave that with them. Now, on the transfer thing, just so I have it straight. Is it happening on every after-hours call that hits the AI agent and then goes to a live rep?

27
00:03:32.233 --> 00:03:39.668
Luis Ortega: Every one we've checked. It doesn't seem to matter which queue or which rep. The details just don't land.

28
00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:48.195
Rachel Okafor: Understood. I'll open a case and keep you posted. In the meantime, are your reps working around it somehow?

29
00:03:48.571 --> 00:03:59.014
Luis Ortega: They're just asking the caller to repeat themselves. It's not the end of the world, but it's not great for the member experience either.

30
00:03:59.952 --> 00:04:11.587
Rachel Okafor: Yeah, I get that. I'll flag it with the product team and see what we can find. Probably need the call IDs before I can say much more.

31
00:04:13.075 --> 00:04:16.039
Luis Ortega: Fair enough. I'll send those over today.

32
00:04:16.494 --> 00:04:25.375
Rachel Okafor: Thanks. Before I let you go, is there anything else on your list? Anything coming up that I should know about?

33
00:04:25.858 --> 00:04:37.941
Luis Ortega: Not really. We're in good shape otherwise. The only thing is my director wants a quick readout on the pilot by mid-October, so if you have any early data, that'd help.

34
00:04:38.458 --> 00:04:44.949
Rachel Okafor: I can put together a short summary from the dashboards. What kind of numbers does she want to see?

35
00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:52.213
Luis Ortega: Containment rate, average handle time, and how many calls the AI is catching after hours. Just a page or so.

36
00:04:52.587 --> 00:05:01.681
Rachel Okafor: Got it. I'll have something for you the week of the fifth. That gives us a little buffer before your deadline.

37
00:05:02.036 --> 00:05:02.836
Luis Ortega: That works.

38
00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:14.278
Rachel Okafor: Okay, so to recap, I'll open the case on the transfer details, you'll send call IDs today, and I'll send a pilot summary in early October.

39
00:05:15.458 --> 00:05:16.785
Luis Ortega: Sounds right. Thanks Rachel.

40
00:05:17.826 --> 00:05:22.690
Rachel Okafor: Any time. I'll follow up by Monday either way. Have a good one, Luis.

41
00:05:24.174 --> 00:05:25.720
Luis Ortega: You too. Talk soon.
